# Detail page standard

This is a premium product for Indian schools. Open the page on localhost and look at it before calling the work done.

## Verify
- Load the real record (not a mock). Confirm every field comes from the API.
- Blank email/mobile/usage after onboarding is a mapping bug, not an empty-state.
- If two sections show the same plan, code, or status, delete one.

## What to show
Shape the page from the **Add** form, not from leftover tabs:
- Identity (name lives in the shell; status + one-line plan/admin on a compact row)
- Organization basics captured at create (short name, type, domain, address, timezone, currency, language)
- Dedicated admin/contact block (name, email, mobile)
- Linked parent (customer, class, etc.) with **View details →**
- Commercial block (plan, invoice generated from the subscription, trial vs paid, amount paid, coupon)
- Entitlements + live usage vs plan limits (snapshot from backend, refreshed daily)
- Tenant/ops (schema, DB size, URL, SSL, maintenance, migration) only once
- Recent activity from real events (created, provisioned, subscription, backup)

Prefer **one scrolling page**. Tabs only if each tab has unique data and zero repeats.

## Layout
- `tc-saas-page-header` is actions only: Back, Edit, overflow Actions with tooltips.
- Tight gaps (~0.7rem). Cards shrink to content. Do not stretch empty columns.
- No KPI hero, no second copy of the org code, no Suspend button outside Actions.

## Edit
- Edit navigates to the Add form titled **Edit {Entity}**.
- Disable immutable fields (customer, domain, original subscription).
- Keep admin email/mobile, name, address, logo enabled when those are allowed to change.

## Do not
- Hardcode students/staff/storage percentages or invoice amounts
- Repeat the same fact on two tabs or two cards
- Invent actions without a tooltip
- Ship without opening localhost
